message: >-
  If you use vep-rs in your work, please cite the software (this file) and, once
  it is published, the article named in the README's Citing section.
type: software
title: vep-rs
abstract: >-
  vep-rs is a fast, memory-efficient variant effect predictor written in Rust.
  It annotates genomic variants with their predicted functional effects on
  genes, transcripts, and protein sequences, implementing the Ensembl Variant
  Effect Predictor (VEP) algorithm, reading a JSON transcript cache built from
  Ensembl release files or converted from an Ensembl VEP cache, and producing
  compatible output. Its concordance with Ensembl VEP release 116.2 is measured
  on the whole genome: 11,838,755,797 VEP consequence tuples from gnomAD, 1000
  Genomes and ClinVar data on GRCh37 and GRCh38, reported per dataset, with raw
  F1 of at least 0.999972446 on each of the six whole-genome datasets and
  adjusted F1 of 1.000000000 on every dataset and every structural-variant file
  set once the documented divergence classes are set aside. Wall time is
  measured on the whole genome on five independently provisioned machines per
  chromosome and architecture and stated beside Ensembl VEP's and fastVEP's.
  Every published aggregate re-derives from the provenance records released with
  the code, and the intended-divergences page documents every class set aside.
